1
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:04,390
<i>Hajime Suzuki, high school sophomore.</i>

2
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:06,610
<i>My genre of choice is BL.</i>

3
00:00:06,610 --> 00:00:08,360
<i>I'm currently writing a BL novel,</i>

4
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:13,640
<i>using the ever popular Serizawa, as my model.</i>

5
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,500
It's definitely over here.

6
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,280
You sure? You were wrong yesterday.

7
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:21,570
Is the "Haruto Serizawa" written here, me?

8
00:00:21,570 --> 00:00:24,370
Does that mean you like me, Suzuki?

9
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:26,100
<i>It's so over.</i>

10
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:27,080
I'm sorry!

11
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:30,710
My romantic orientation

12
00:00:30,710 --> 00:00:33,960
has nothing to do with my BL hobby.

13
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:39,480
I never looked at you in that way.

14
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:40,830
I see.

15
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:43,340
Then let me read it.

16
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:44,940
That novel of yours.

17
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:46,130
Huh?

18
00:00:46,130 --> 00:00:48,820
Give me the honor

19
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,680
of being your first reader.

20
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:57,380
<i>This was how Serizawa began reading my novel.</i>

21
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:32,880
Huh?

22
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:34,780
That's it?

23
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,740
Yeah.

24
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:40,820
I haven't written more.

25
00:01:42,010 --> 00:01:46,730
Sorry, I know it's bad.

26
00:01:46,730 --> 00:01:50,940
You left it at such a cliffhanger...

27
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:53,870
Wait, you think it's interesting?

28
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:54,860
Yeah.

29
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:56,560
The bottom's likable?

30
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:58,450
Is the top suave?

31
00:01:58,450 --> 00:01:59,570
Totally.

32
00:01:59,570 --> 00:02:03,340
And I think the bottom is adorable.

33
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:06,250
What a relief.

34
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:08,300
Thanks for the feedback.

35
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:11,210
It helps that you have such a model top.

36
00:02:11,210 --> 00:02:13,750
Can't deny that.

37
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:16,220
So, when will you write the rest?

38
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:21,000
I usually write during these breaks,
or at home.

39
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,410
On your phone?

40
00:02:22,410 --> 00:02:25,100
- Yeah.
- I see.

41
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:27,880
Then don't let me stop you. Here.

42
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:30,610
- Now?
- Yeah, now.

43
00:02:35,490 --> 00:02:38,330
Okay, sure.

44
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:48,740
You're going to watch me?

45
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:51,090
Yeah. I need to know what happens next.

46
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:56,990
Right...

47
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:05,600
I can't really see your screen.

48
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:10,600
Wait, I got it. Suzuki.

49
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,350
Sit here.

50
00:03:12,350 --> 00:03:13,550
Huh?

51
00:03:13,550 --> 00:03:16,670
Then I can read over your shoulder.

52
00:03:16,670 --> 00:03:19,700
Isn't it weird if I sat there?

53
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:22,400
What? No, it isn't.

54
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:24,250
Come on, don't be shy.

55
00:03:30,110 --> 00:03:32,890
How's that feel?

56
00:03:32,890 --> 00:03:34,690
Comfortable?

57
00:03:37,870 --> 00:03:40,030
I guess...

58
00:03:40,030 --> 00:03:43,270
Perfect. Now get writing

59
00:03:43,270 --> 00:03:45,380
for your very first reader,

60
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:47,350
Mr. Suzuki.

61
00:04:34,770 --> 00:04:36,450
[Episode 2]

62
00:04:36,450 --> 00:04:39,090
- Serizawa.
- Yeah?

63
00:04:39,090 --> 00:04:41,600
We definitely look strange right now.

64
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,950
- You think?
- Yes?

65
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:45,750
I mean, if anyone saw us...

66
00:04:45,750 --> 00:04:47,020
Serizawa.

67
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:49,490
I bought whatever you asked for...

68
00:04:50,970 --> 00:04:54,230
- What're you two doing?
- Lunchtime!

69
00:04:54,230 --> 00:04:56,370
- Uh...
- Huh?

70
00:04:56,370 --> 00:04:59,010
Suzuki? 'Sup.

71
00:05:00,430 --> 00:05:02,220
Why does Serizawa have you in his clutches?

72
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:04,650
He's not "in my clutches".

73
00:05:04,650 --> 00:05:06,740
We're getting along just fine.

74
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:09,090
You clearly pushed him into this.

75
00:05:09,090 --> 00:05:10,870
I did not.

76
00:05:10,870 --> 00:05:13,200
Right, Suzuki?

77
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:16,750
Well, I mean...

78
00:05:18,230 --> 00:05:20,290
Whatever, I'm starving.

79
00:05:20,290 --> 00:05:23,150
Same, let's eat.

80
00:05:23,150 --> 00:05:25,320
Lunch is always the best time of day.

81
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:28,910
What did she pack today...

82
00:05:28,910 --> 00:05:30,600
Woah, what a feast!

83
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:31,720
Let me see.

84
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:34,130
- Your girlfriend's cooking?
- Yup.

85
00:05:34,130 --> 00:05:37,290
- Give me a bite.
- Hey!

86
00:05:38,330 --> 00:05:41,420
Serizawa, I should get going...

87
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:43,280
Suzuki.

88
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:45,650
Here.

89
00:05:45,650 --> 00:05:47,300
Huh?

90
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:49,920
Don't worry, I bought your share.

91
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,110
No, we did.

92
00:05:51,110 --> 00:05:53,910
Well, I'm the one who paid.

93
00:05:53,910 --> 00:05:56,160
- Don't get it twisted.
- Hah!

94
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:58,590
You and your way of stating the obvious.

95
00:05:58,590 --> 00:06:01,420
That's Serizawa grammar for you.

96
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:03,150
What'll you have, Suzuki?

97
00:06:03,150 --> 00:06:07,960
I bought bread and rice, so take your pick.

98
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:11,040
Then I'll take a rice ball.

99
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:12,510
Sure.

100
00:06:13,260 --> 00:06:14,400
Here.

101
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:16,510
Th-Thanks.

102
00:06:16,510 --> 00:06:18,580
I'll pay you back later.

103
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:20,000
Don't worry about it.

104
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,650
It's my treat, Mr. Suzuki.

105
00:06:22,650 --> 00:06:24,800
- "Mister"?
- Serizawa!

106
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:26,420
I know, I know.

107
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:31,460
It's our secret.

108
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:34,050
- No need to show off.
- Yeah, man.

109
00:06:34,050 --> 00:06:35,140
Seriously.

110
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:36,610
So, what're you having?

111
00:06:36,610 --> 00:06:38,100
- Fried chicken.
- Chicken?

112
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,910
- Don't.
- Come on, please?

113
00:06:39,910 --> 00:06:41,800
- Serizawa.
- Yeah?

114
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:43,100
Could we...

115
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:45,160
- Sure.
- How about some crab sticks?

116
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:48,360
- Not interested.
- Why am I not surprised.

117
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:53,080
What's up?

118
00:06:53,820 --> 00:06:56,680
Just to make sure...

119
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,550
You haven't told the others

120
00:06:59,550 --> 00:07:03,890
about my love for BL, right?

121
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:07,940
Yeah, of course not.

122
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:10,350
Okay, good.

123
00:07:10,350 --> 00:07:13,110
I don't think they'd care though.

124
00:07:13,110 --> 00:07:16,090
No, you can't. Promise you won't tell.

125
00:07:17,850 --> 00:07:20,810
Okay. If you'd rather I didn't, then I won't.

126
00:07:21,810 --> 00:07:24,350
It'll be our little secret.

127
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:28,260
Yeah. Thanks.

128
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:37,640
In exchange...

129
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:42,500
Come have lunch with me from now on.

130
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:44,190
Every day?

131
00:07:44,190 --> 00:07:48,000
Yup. I want to read your newest updates.

132
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:52,140
Please, Mr. Suzuki?

133
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:56,280
<i>And so,</i>

134
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:58,600
<i>one week passed.</i>

135
00:08:00,290 --> 00:08:04,080
What should I start with?

136
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:09,680
<i>I got into a routine of having lunch
with the popular kids.</i>

137
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:15,210
Suzuki, open wide.

138
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:21,260
<i>Or more accurately, I'm being fed lunch.</i>

139
00:08:21,260 --> 00:08:23,220
How's that taste?

140
00:08:23,220 --> 00:08:25,540
Good, but...

141
00:08:26,270 --> 00:08:28,170
Dude, what are you doing?

142
00:08:28,170 --> 00:08:29,850
My question exactly.

143
00:08:29,850 --> 00:08:32,150
I knew this was weird, Serizawa.

144
00:08:32,150 --> 00:08:35,580
Don't mind them.

145
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:39,200
Here, open wide.

146
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:46,390
Suzuki, what is he even making you do?

147
00:08:46,390 --> 00:08:48,540
Is he blackmailing you?

148
00:08:48,540 --> 00:08:51,670
If he's bothering you, tell us.

149
00:08:51,670 --> 00:08:53,730
Otherwise, this selfish brat won't stop.

150
00:08:53,730 --> 00:08:56,530
Don't bother him!

151
00:08:56,530 --> 00:09:00,060
I'm improving Suzuki's efficiency.

152
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:02,030
It's my patented Serizawa Way.

153
00:09:02,030 --> 00:09:03,810
Huh?

154
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:08,600
The Serizawa Way, is it?

155
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:12,630
<i>Lately, I've begun to realize...</i>

156
00:09:12,630 --> 00:09:15,850
<i>Serizawa acts weird around me.</i>

157
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:21,440
Let's start with warm-ups.

158
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:23,480
Suzuki.

159
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:25,380
Let's partner up again.

160
00:09:26,850 --> 00:09:28,860
Sure.

161
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:30,800
Suzuki!

162
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:32,870
Let's walk home together.

163
00:09:32,870 --> 00:09:34,300
Uh...

164
00:09:38,230 --> 00:09:43,040
I take a right here. See you tomorrow.

165
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:45,030
Suzuki, wait.

166
00:09:45,030 --> 00:09:48,240
Let's trade contact info.

167
00:09:49,870 --> 00:09:53,210
<i>Yeah, something's definitely up.</i>

168
00:09:56,930 --> 00:10:02,410
<i>Another day of Serizawa attached to my hip...</i>

169
00:10:07,790 --> 00:10:10,130
<i>Suzuki, you asleep?</i>

170
00:10:10,130 --> 00:10:12,110
<i>If you're awake, let's talk.</i>

171
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,640
Talk?

172
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:17,160
Like, on the phone?

173
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:19,400
Or does he mean a video call?

174
00:10:22,180 --> 00:10:24,380
No, no way.

175
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:26,320
What should I do?

176
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:32,500
<i>Night, Suzuki.</i>

177
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:34,250
<i>I'll see you tomorrow.</i>

178
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:44,630
<i>Why is Serizawa so interested in me?</i>

179
00:10:45,550 --> 00:10:48,670
I wonder if I should respond...

180
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,810
But...

181
00:10:54,570 --> 00:10:56,640
I don't know.

182
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:14,300
Good morning, Mr. Suzuki.

183
00:11:14,300 --> 00:11:15,940
You scared me.

184
00:11:15,940 --> 00:11:17,280
Good morning.

185
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:18,860
Morning.

186
00:11:19,630 --> 00:11:21,890
You look tired.

187
00:11:23,010 --> 00:11:24,560
Yeah.

188
00:11:25,390 --> 00:11:27,640
I wasn't able to sleep well last night.

189
00:11:27,640 --> 00:11:30,100
I ended up passing the time by reading.

190
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:32,650
So, you were awake!

191
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:34,970
Sorry, I should've responded.

192
00:11:34,970 --> 00:11:36,360
What did you need?

193
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:38,480
Nothing much.

194
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:41,820
I just wanted to hear your voice.

195
00:11:41,820 --> 00:11:43,240
Huh?

196
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:45,360
Oh hey, we have home economics today.

197
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:49,010
It's gonna be fun, cooking together.

198
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:56,850
Serizawa...

199
00:11:56,850 --> 00:11:58,270
Yeah?

200
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:02,280
Never mind.

201
00:12:03,850 --> 00:12:06,120
Suzuki? Hey, wait up!

202
00:12:07,550 --> 00:12:11,620
Today we'll be making
stewed chicken and vegetables.

203
00:12:11,620 --> 00:12:14,420
- A stew...
- That's right.

204
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:15,850
You got all the ingredients?

205
00:12:15,850 --> 00:12:17,370
- Yes, ma'am.
- Great.

206
00:12:17,370 --> 00:12:19,910
Then let's get cooking.

207
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:30,410
Serizawa?

208
00:12:32,580 --> 00:12:35,040
Suzuki.

209
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:38,640
I'm a heroic sort of top, right?

210
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:40,240
Huh?

211
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:46,640
I mean,

212
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:50,770
you are in my mind.

213
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:53,910
And in my mind,

214
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:58,310
most tops are great cooks.

215
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:02,970
I agree with you there.

216
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:08,560
All right then. Leave it to me, Suzuki.

217
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:11,980
I'm going to be the King of Stewing!

218
00:13:11,980 --> 00:13:13,460
Huh?

219
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:16,860
What are you talking about?

220
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:18,810
I'm going to be the Stewing King.

221
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:25,620
You haven't managed to shape one?

222
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:28,090
It's been minutes.

223
00:13:28,090 --> 00:13:30,440
Meanwhile, look at Takeuchi's plate.

224
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:32,130
- It's simple.
- He's so speedy.

225
00:13:32,130 --> 00:13:33,850
- Like a pro.
- Woah.

226
00:13:33,850 --> 00:13:36,200
I'm more impressed by Serizawa's disaster.

227
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:39,670
There.

228
00:13:46,050 --> 00:13:49,120
You didn't manage to make a single slice.

229
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:51,170
We don't even need green onion.

230
00:13:51,170 --> 00:13:53,970
- Huh?
- It's not called for in the recipe.

231
00:13:53,970 --> 00:13:55,240
Then why'd you bring one?

232
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:57,400
- Huh?
- Dude.

233
00:14:03,330 --> 00:14:04,780
Like a pencil.

234
00:14:04,780 --> 00:14:06,980
This guy cannot cook for his life.

235
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:09,610
"King of Stewing", my butt.

236
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:13,640
I'll take over, Serizawa.

237
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:18,230
You've got a ways to go, man.

238
00:14:18,230 --> 00:14:20,540
Yeah, about 3,000 miles left, I'd say.

239
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:23,670
- He slumped down.
- You made him depressed.

240
00:14:23,670 --> 00:14:25,330
Aren't you going to become the King of Stewing?

241
00:14:25,330 --> 00:14:26,910
- Come on!
- Don't give up now!

242
00:14:26,910 --> 00:14:28,800
Stand, Serizawa!

243
00:14:31,010 --> 00:14:34,040
- Give up on that carrot, though.
- Yeah...

244
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:39,050
Give your meals a try. Bon appétit!

245
00:14:39,050 --> 00:14:42,950
Bon appétit!

246
00:14:42,950 --> 00:14:44,960
Let's see how it tastes.

247
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:48,430
- Everyone got their chopsticks?
- Yeah.

248
00:14:52,780 --> 00:14:54,740
That's good.

249
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:58,640
Yeah, Suzuki's stock is really flavorful.

250
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:02,170
And Suzuki's carrots

251
00:15:02,170 --> 00:15:04,420
were cut to perfection.

252
00:15:04,420 --> 00:15:09,220
I'm glad our group had Suzuki to help.

253
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:10,880
Yeah.

254
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:12,870
Agreed.

255
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:16,690
If you three keep complaining,

256
00:15:16,690 --> 00:15:18,550
then our group's gonna split.

257
00:15:18,550 --> 00:15:20,070
Sounds good to me.

258
00:15:20,070 --> 00:15:22,870
I wasn't ever a part of any group.

259
00:15:22,870 --> 00:15:25,150
You're our weak link anyway.

260
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:28,190
Saeki, come here.

261
00:15:28,190 --> 00:15:32,120
- Koharu's stew is seriously good.
- Ignore them.

262
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:34,530
- Trust us.
- Nope, don't.

263
00:15:34,530 --> 00:15:36,490
- Let me try.
- Stop it!

264
00:15:36,490 --> 00:15:38,350
- Why not?
- Bon appétit!

265
00:15:38,350 --> 00:15:41,300
Guys, I said don't!

266
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:43,550
You three weren't invited!

267
00:15:43,550 --> 00:15:46,490
Sorry, Suzuki.

268
00:15:47,590 --> 00:15:49,310
What?

269
00:15:50,110 --> 00:15:53,420
I'm supposed to be a heroic top,

270
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:55,550
yet I can't even cook.

271
00:15:56,740 --> 00:16:00,770
Don't let it bother you.

272
00:16:00,770 --> 00:16:05,480
But I wanted to become the ideal top.

273
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:12,650
Well...

274
00:16:12,650 --> 00:16:15,270
You can practice.

275
00:16:15,270 --> 00:16:17,390
Huh?

276
00:16:17,390 --> 00:16:23,090
I mean, not every top starts out perfect.

277
00:16:23,090 --> 00:16:25,160
Really?

278
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:28,020
You think I can become the King of Stewing?

279
00:16:28,020 --> 00:16:31,990
Yeah, I do.

280
00:16:31,990 --> 00:16:33,940
So, don't be so down.

281
00:16:33,940 --> 00:16:35,420
Okay?

282
00:16:40,220 --> 00:16:43,220
Sorry! I didn't mean to act so patronizing!

283
00:16:43,220 --> 00:16:44,800
You weren't.

284
00:16:46,570 --> 00:16:49,790
Thanks.

285
00:16:49,790 --> 00:16:52,020
I feel much better now.

286
00:16:54,450 --> 00:16:56,280
You do?

287
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:58,210
Then I'm glad it worked.

288
00:16:59,830 --> 00:17:03,020
Hey, let's take a selfie together.

289
00:17:03,020 --> 00:17:05,040
- A selfie?
- Yeah.

290
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:07,290
Get our cooking in the picture, too.

291
00:17:07,290 --> 00:17:09,590
You sure?

292
00:17:14,350 --> 00:17:16,330
Yeah. Now smile!

293
00:17:17,030 --> 00:17:19,350
Say cheese!

294
00:17:20,420 --> 00:17:22,210
Let me get another one.

295
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:24,850
Ready?

296
00:17:24,850 --> 00:17:27,280
Say cheese!

297
00:17:36,130 --> 00:17:39,950
Cooking together was fun,

298
00:17:39,950 --> 00:17:44,240
but it's too bad I couldn't read
your newest update today.

299
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:50,550
<i>Oh, right.</i>

300
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:53,390
<i>I should've known.</i>

301
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:00,460
<i>Thanks for cheering me up today!</i>

302
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:03,860
<i>I'm going to become the King of Stewing!</i>

303
00:18:05,570 --> 00:18:09,420
<i>I'm not the one</i>

304
00:18:09,420 --> 00:18:12,410
<i>Serizawa is interested in.</i>

305
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:18,420
<i>Can't wait to read
more of your novel tomorrow!</i>

306
00:18:28,710 --> 00:18:31,910
[Plot Journal]

307
00:18:40,750 --> 00:18:44,240
Suzuki. Let's walk home together.

308
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:45,680
Yeah.

309
00:18:52,550 --> 00:18:55,030
Serizawa.

310
00:18:55,030 --> 00:18:56,470
What's up?

311
00:18:58,200 --> 00:19:03,220
There's something I need to tell you.

312
00:19:04,450 --> 00:19:05,850
Okay.

313
00:19:17,810 --> 00:19:19,680
Serizawa.

314
00:19:20,770 --> 00:19:22,410
I'm sorry.

315
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:28,170
Huh? What's up?

316
00:19:30,170 --> 00:19:34,790
The novel you're reading right now.

317
00:19:37,060 --> 00:19:41,320
I probably won't ever finish it.

318
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:42,790
What?

319
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:46,300
To tell you the truth...

320
00:19:47,850 --> 00:19:49,610
[Plot Journal]

321
00:19:51,410 --> 00:19:54,090
<i>I've never managed to finish a novel.</i>

322
00:19:54,090 --> 00:19:56,440
Not a single one.

323
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:00,650
When I write alone,

324
00:20:01,350 --> 00:20:04,510
I get lost somewhere along the way.

325
00:20:04,510 --> 00:20:07,750
I never know if my writing is interesting,

326
00:20:07,750 --> 00:20:10,300
and I tend to give up before I finish.

327
00:20:12,510 --> 00:20:16,880
So, if I lose heart on this work as well,

328
00:20:17,620 --> 00:20:20,370
I'd feel bad about leaving you hanging.

329
00:20:24,150 --> 00:20:25,710
Serizawa.

330
00:20:26,720 --> 00:20:30,510
I'm not worthy of your respect at all.

331
00:20:33,510 --> 00:20:37,060
What, that's it?

332
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:38,370
Huh?

333
00:20:38,370 --> 00:20:40,690
You had me spooked.

334
00:20:40,690 --> 00:20:42,770
I thought my cooking was so bad,

335
00:20:42,770 --> 00:20:46,260
you became disillusioned with me as a top.

336
00:20:46,260 --> 00:20:48,330
What?

337
00:20:48,330 --> 00:20:50,330
If anything,

338
00:20:50,330 --> 00:20:54,290
I respect you even more now.

339
00:20:54,290 --> 00:20:56,970
I mean, you never gave up, right?

340
00:20:56,970 --> 00:21:00,930
No matter how many times you lost heart,

341
00:21:00,930 --> 00:21:04,110
you still continued to write.

342
00:21:04,740 --> 00:21:08,310
That's seriously amazing, you know?

343
00:21:11,230 --> 00:21:13,340
Besides.

344
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:21,170
You're not writing alone now.

345
00:21:21,990 --> 00:21:23,530
What?

346
00:21:24,980 --> 00:21:27,190
Suzuki.

347
00:21:27,190 --> 00:21:31,000
If you ever get lost in your writing,

348
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:33,100
talk to me about it.

349
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:37,040
I'll come to help, no matter where I am.

350
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:40,860
I'll tell you everything
I like about your writing,

351
00:21:40,860 --> 00:21:45,700
until it's hammered into your head, okay?

352
00:21:48,910 --> 00:21:51,020
Serizawa...

353
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:54,850
Pinky promise.

354
00:22:11,360 --> 00:22:15,310
In the meantime, I'll work hard
on becoming the King of Stewing.

355
00:22:15,310 --> 00:22:17,380
You were serious about that?

356
00:22:17,380 --> 00:22:20,330
Of course.

357
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,920
And this picture proves it.

358
00:22:26,420 --> 00:22:29,360
Hey! Delete that!

359
00:22:29,360 --> 00:22:30,350
Not happening.

360
00:22:30,350 --> 00:22:31,790
You're being selfish again.

361
00:22:31,790 --> 00:22:34,460
- Stop!
- Suzuki?

362
00:22:34,460 --> 00:22:36,300
Something up, Matsuno?

363
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:41,300
Hey, isn't that Suzuki?

364
00:22:41,300 --> 00:22:43,030
And Serizawa.

365
00:22:43,030 --> 00:22:45,750
Why's Suzuki hanging out with him?

366
00:22:50,390 --> 00:22:52,280
Just delete it.

367
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:53,350
- Delete it.
- Nope.

368
00:22:53,350 --> 00:22:55,460
- Delete it.
- Nuh-uh.

369
00:22:55,460 --> 00:22:57,780
Come on, please?

370
00:22:57,780 --> 00:22:59,920
Nope.

371
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:03,690
Suzupi, how'd you get so close
with Serizawa's group?

372
00:23:03,690 --> 00:23:04,900
There you are.

373
00:23:04,900 --> 00:23:06,490
Join us for karaoke.

374
00:23:06,490 --> 00:23:09,160
I've never sung in front of other people.

375
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:11,400
Seriously?

376
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:13,390
I think I can sing.

377
00:23:13,390 --> 00:23:15,000
Sorry, never mind!

